<title>BELGIUM: Solvay to invest $25 mln in Bulgarian unit Sodi.</title>
<headline>Solvay to invest $25 mln in Bulgarian unit Sodi.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solvay Sodi JSCO, a Bulgarian unit of Belgian chemical and pharmaceutical group Solvay, will invest 40 billion leva ($25 million) in its soda ash plant at Devnya, Solvay said in a statement on Sunday.</p>
<p>The investment will allow the company to double its dense soda ash capacity to 800,000 tonnes per year. It is expected to be completed by the last quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>Solvay owns 66.7 percent of the Bulgarian firm.</p>
</text>
